                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">"Drug-Induced Diseases" is an interdisciplinary course between medicine and pharmacy, which aims to systematically introduce drug-induced diseases that may be caused during drug use, as well as their pathogenic mechanisms, clinical manifestations, diagnosis, prevention and treatment. In addition to providing theoretical knowledge, this course also helps students master the clinical identification and treatment of drug-induced diseases through case analysis. Through the study of this course, students can apply the knowledge they have learned to reasonably guide clinical drug use, reduce the occurrence of drug-induced diseases, reduce the degree of drug-induced diseases, and ensure the safety of patients' medication.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
